{"type":"message","id":"9650497a","parentId":"0bc7231d","timestamp":"2026-02-23T21:39:54.132Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've successfully distilled the key learnings from the recent memory files into MEMORY.md. Now let me create a summary of what was done for the cron task output.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"## Memory Maintenance Complete ✅\n\nSuccessfully distilled key learnings, decisions, and context from the past 8 days into MEMORY.md.\n\n### Summary of Updates:\n\n**Key Sections Added/Updated:**\n1. **User Profile** - Sam's communication preferences (frustrated with context memory issues)\n2. **System Architecture** - OpenClaw v2026.2.21-2, model routing (GLM primary, Codex fallback), cron jobs status\n3. **Automation & Integrations** - GitHub backup, Notion API, Tavily search configurations\n4. **Critical Issues** - Memory system problems (context contamination), Telegram delivery failures, CLI PATH issues\n5. **Identity & Persona** - Hugin (🦉) from Antigravity (🌌)\n6. **Security Context** - CVE-2025-24813 overdue, false positives catalogued\n7. **Project History** - Design work, model testing, subagent pairing issues\n8. **Technical Notes** - WSL2 Node 22+ IPv6 troubleshooting, WAL system (with warning not to over-explain)\n\n### Important Discoveries:\n- **Memory System Problem:** Agent repeatedly responding about WAL when user didn't ask - indicates context tracking failure\n- **Cron Tasks Working:** All scheduled jobs execute successfully, only Telegram \"announce\" delivery fails\n- **CLI Path Issue:** Daily security audit's deep scan fails because `openclaw` not in PATH (npx installation)\n- **Model Routing:** Aggressive mode confirmed as user preference - spawn Codex for almost all non-trivial work\n\n### Status:\n- **MEMORY.md:** 8,820 bytes, fully curated\n- **Entries Processed:** 7 daily memory files (Feb 16-23)\n- **Key Insights Captured:** System architecture,